If your laptop is shut down, your deployed Render app will still keep working. You do not need to start Django locally just to use the live website.
For the deployed app, after restarting your laptop, simply open:
Frontend:
https://smart-web-notes.onrender.com

Backend admin:
https://smart-web-notes-backend.onrender.com/admin/

No CMD commands are required.
If you want to continue local development, then start frontend and backend again.
1. Backend — open CMD:
cd "D:\Dhananjay AWS\Django Projects\smart-web-notes\backend"
.venv\Scripts\activate
python manage.py runserver

Then local backend/admin works at:
http://127.0.0.1:8000/
http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/

2. Frontend — open a second CMD window:
cd "D:\Dhananjay AWS\Django Projects\smart-web-notes\frontend"
npm start

or:
ng serve

Then open:
http://localhost:4200/